# What `docker context inspect --format` answers, as TestDockerEnvironment's DockerContextEndpoint
# asks it: the endpoint, a bar, then `tls` when the context carries TLS material.
# One section per answer: its lines up to the blank line that separates it from the next one.
# `docker` is the answer of a link found by its bare name on a PATH, which must be named after
# the binary itself (TestDockerEnvironmentFunctionalSpec, build-logic).

[unix-socket]
unix:///run/stand-in/docker.sock|

[ssh-host]
ssh://builder@docker.invalid|

[tls-context]
tcp://docker.invalid:2376|tls

[docker]
unix:///run/stand-in/path-docker.sock|
